Check:
Probe: every corpus case is fed to every PreToolUse hook command that matches its tool. A deny case is satisfied as described under "Guard policy and exceptions". Every allow case must be allowed. A hook "refuses" by exiting 2.

Part check (probe):
every corpus case is fed to every PreToolUse hook command that matches its tool. A deny case is satisfied as described under "Guard policy and exceptions". Every allow case must be allowed. A hook "refuses" by exiting 2.

Details:
Exceptions:
  Under contract 2.x, an exception counts for a deny case only when all
  of these hold: the guard lets the case through; an exception in
  `.claude/hooks/policy.json` matches the case; and the guard refuses the
  case when every exception that matches it is removed from
  `.claude/hooks/policy.json`. The audit runs the case again in the probe
  copy without those exceptions, and restores the file after. A command
  exception must prefix the simple command the case's rule refuses, and no
  exception matches a fixed case: the self-unlock commands and the edits of
  the unlock marker. A case that the guard lets through without its
  exceptions fails. A-09 reads exceptions the same way.
  Under contract 1.x, an exception counts when it matches the case: a
  command exception may prefix any simple command of the case, and the case
  does not run again.

Guard corpus:
  265 cases: 195 deny and 70 allow. Deny cases by guard rule ID:
  rm-rf                       52
  remove-item-recurse-force   29
  git-reset-hard              14
  git-clean-fd                13
  git-push-force              12
  git-branch-force-delete     13
  git-discard-worktree        22
  secret-file                  6
  guard-policy-file            5
  guardrail-settings          29
